boh — third-party components
============================

boh itself is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

The published container image bundles the following third-party software.
These are separate works, distributed alongside boh as mere aggregation;
each remains under its own license.


Bundled in the container image
------------------------------

gallery-dl — GPL-2.0
    https://github.com/mikf/gallery-dl
    Invoked by boh as a separate process via the command line. boh links no
    gallery-dl code into its own binaries.

FFmpeg — LGPL-2.1-or-later / GPL-2.0-or-later depending on build configuration
    https://ffmpeg.org
    Provided by the Debian `ffmpeg` package. Invoked as a separate process for
    video thumbnail extraction and media probing.

Python — PSF License
    https://docs.python.org/3/license.html
    Runtime dependency of gallery-dl.


Referenced as package / source dependencies
-------------------------------------------

Magick.NET (ImageMagick) — Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/dlemstra/Magick.NET
    https://imagemagick.org/script/license.php
    Used for still-image decoding, probing and thumbnail generation. The
    Q8-AnyCPU package bundles the native ImageMagick libraries.

Pico CSS — MIT
    https://github.com/picocss/pico

htmx — Zero-Clause BSD (0BSD)
    https://github.com/bigskysoftware/htmx

Entity Framework Core, ASP.NET Core — MIT
    https://github.com/dotnet/efcore
    https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore

BCrypt.Net-Next — MIT
    https://github.com/BcryptNet/bcrypt.net

SQLitePCLRaw — Apache-2.0, bundling SQLite (public domain)
    https://github.com/ericsink/SQLitePCL.raw
    https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html
    Pinned ahead of the version Entity Framework Core resolves, to pick up a
    SQLite release containing the fix for CVE-2025-6965.


Colour schemes
--------------

The packaged themes in src/Boh.Web/wwwroot/css/themes.css are adapted from the
schemes below. They are derived works, not copies: each upstream palette is
built for syntax highlighting on a single background, and individual tones were
shifted along their own hue until every pair boh renders as text met WCAG AA.
scripts/build-themes.py records the source values and performs the adaptation.

Nord — MIT
    https://github.com/nordtheme/nord

Dracula — MIT
    https://github.com/dracula/visual-studio-code

Monokai — MIT
    https://github.com/microsoft/vscode (extensions/theme-monokai)
    Based on the original scheme by Wimer Hazenberg.

Gruvbox — MIT
    https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox
    Declared in the project's package.json; the repository carries no LICENSE file.

Catppuccin — MIT
    https://github.com/catppuccin/palette

Solarized — MIT
    https://github.com/altercation/solarized
